  warn Name collision on `*:9442`: `@ROOT@/B/httpd.conf:27` never gets its name `dup.test`, which `@ROOT@/B/httpd.conf:21` takes. Apache picks the first virtual host that matches a name, so a virtual host is never served for a name another one takes, yet Apache still loads its certificate on every reload. Give each virtual host names of its own.
